{
  "//": "Markup-fidelity fixture for the composite-badge component — the three-part `.pa-composite-badge` block ([icon][label][button]) that keen `composite_badge/1` and svelte `CompositeBadge.svelte` render. SCOPE = IN-SCOPE / SELF-CONTAINED (NOT container-only like prop-card). Unlike prop-card — whose rows are a separate sub-component fed via a slot — the composite badge renders its own `__icon` / `__label` / `__button` parts INLINE from flat string/slot props (labelText + buttonText + optional icon). There is no composite-badge-row sub-component; the three parts ARE the component's markup, so they're modelled as features and exercised directly in the goldens (nothing deferred). Wrapper dumpers map `props` to their own API, render, and the core comparator diffs their output against `golden` after normalization. See ../README.md and badge.json for the model, prop-card.json for the container-only counter-example.",
  "component": "composite-badge",
  "block": "pa-composite-badge",
  "propsVocabulary": {
    "variant": "base colour variant (primary|secondary|success|warning|danger|info|light|dark) — paints all three sections. On the block as pa-composite-badge--{variant}",
    "labelVariant": "override the LABEL section's colour independently of the base variant — pa-composite-badge--label-{v} (svelte labelVariant, keen label_variant)",
    "buttonVariant": "override the BUTTON section's colour independently — pa-composite-badge--btn-{v} (svelte buttonVariant, keen button_variant). All 8 variants exist (incl. --btn-danger; the SCSS @each covers every variant even though the base __button already renders danger-coloured).",
    "iconVariant": "override the ICON section's colour independently — pa-composite-badge--icon-{v} (svelte iconVariant, keen icon_variant)",
    "icon": "glyph/text rendered inside pa-composite-badge__icon (left section). svelte: icon snippet; keen: icon_content slot (the string `icon` attr and the slot both emit the same __icon span)",
    "label": "middle section text — rendered inside pa-composite-badge__label (svelte labelText, keen label)",
    "buttonText": "right section text/count — rendered inside pa-composite-badge__button (svelte buttonText, keen button_text / count)"
  },
  "goldenConventions": "Structural only — the composite badge adds no attribute conventions like button's type. The outer node is a plain <div>; the three sections are plain <span>s (both wrappers emit <span> for the non-interactive default — keen's button is a <span> unless on_button_click is set; svelte's is a <span> unless isInteractive is set; neither click/interactive path is exercised here, so the blessed default is all-spans). A variant modifier is present when its prop is set. Section text is a plain token (Notifications / 5 / ...) so the diff checks structural nesting, not rich content. The icon section is emitted ONLY when an icon is supplied (both wrappers gate it). The __button section is always present in these scenarios because every scenario supplies buttonText (keen gates __button on btn_text; svelte requires buttonText). Attribute + class-token order and whitespace are normalized away, so goldens are written for readability.",
  "features": {
    "//": "Feature->class contract authored from dist/css/main.css (NOT components.json — its static extraction misses the SCSS-@each-generated variant loops). The .pa-composite-badge block has FOUR independent variant axes — full (--{v}), label (--label-{v}), button (--btn-{v}), icon (--icon-{v}) — each generated for all 8 variants (primary secondary success warning danger info light dark), = 32 block modifiers total, exactly the set in main.css. `produces` is a class template with {value}; capability.mjs expands it and cross-checks against main.css AND each wrapper's map + the scenario set. The three element parts (__icon via the icon slot, __label + __button via the label/buttonText string props) are produced/exercised inline — nothing deferred.",
    "variant": {
      "kind": "enum",
      "options": ["primary", "secondary", "success", "warning", "danger", "info", "light", "dark"],
      "produces": "pa-composite-badge--{value}"
    },
    "labelVariant": {
      "kind": "enum",
      "options": ["primary", "secondary", "success", "warning", "danger", "info", "light", "dark"],
      "produces": "pa-composite-badge--label-{value}"
    },
    "buttonVariant": {
      "kind": "enum",
      "options": ["primary", "secondary", "success", "warning", "danger", "info", "light", "dark"],
      "produces": "pa-composite-badge--btn-{value}"
    },
    "iconVariant": {
      "kind": "enum",
      "options": ["primary", "secondary", "success", "warning", "danger", "info", "light", "dark"],
      "produces": "pa-composite-badge--icon-{value}"
    },
    "icon": {
      "kind": "slot",
      "produces": "pa-composite-badge__icon"
    },
    "label": {
      "kind": "string",
      "produces": null,
      "note": "text inside the always-present pa-composite-badge__label element (exercised by every golden)"
    },
    "buttonText": {
      "kind": "string",
      "produces": null,
      "note": "text inside the pa-composite-badge__button element (exercised by every golden)"
    }
  },
  "cssStateClasses": {
    "//": "pa-composite-badge--* classes in main.css that are NOT feature-driven props in this slice. None — all 32 block modifiers are feature-driven."
  },
